<title>NORWAY: POLL-Fokus H1 profit seen higher.</title>
<headline>POLL-Fokus H1 profit seen higher.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fokus Bank, Norway's fourth largest bank, is  expected to post a first-half 1997 pre-tax profit of 327 million crowns,  according to five analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>The corresponding 1996 profit was 261 million crowns.</p>
<p>Three analysts had a hold recommendation on the share and two said  sell.</p>
<p>Fokus will present the figures on August 14.</p>
<p>				   (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>				   Expectations H1 1997</p>
<p>				  Average    Low     High     H1 1996</p>
<p>Net interest</p>
<p> and credit commission	469	460     472	  463</p>
<p> Other operating income     280	265     298	  219</p>
<p> Operating expenses	   425	409     437	  406</p>
<p>Operating result</p>
<p> before losses/writedowns   323	316     332	  276</p>
<p> Pre-tax result		 327	317     343	  261</p>
<p> EPS (crowns)		   4,96     4,82   5,22</p>
<p> EPS 1997			 8,62     8,00   9,37</p>
<p> EPS 1998			 7,31     6,40   8,00</p>
<p> Dividend 1997		  3,94     3,75   4,00</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, Alf Asklund +47 22 93 69 71</p>
